Public trust lists: the Adobe Approved Trust List and the EU trusted lists
(ETSI TS 119 612, published by the European Commission and the member states)
are downloaded and verified by the application at run time; only SHA-256
fingerprints of their signing certificates are built in.

The offline OpenCerts layouts (core/.../opencerts/OpenCertOffline.kt) follow
the templates of the OpenCerts demo renderer (demo-renderer.opencerts.io,
GovTech Singapore); they were written anew and contain no logos or pictures
from it.

Built-in trust anchors (core/.../trust/BuiltInAnchors.kt,
BuiltInPublicRoots.kt, BuiltInTestAnchors.kt) are public certificates
published by their certification authorities and by the Multipaz project; they
are reproduced for certificate path validation only. The same holds for the
certificates tools/trust-roots keeps in its pinned files (downloaded from each
CA's own site), for the partner CA certificates in
tools/trust-roots/esign-partners (taken from the certificate bundle the e-sign
platform esign.cn publishes for its partner CAs), and for the public service
certificates in test-servers/src/test/resources/chains.

Except for the explicitly attributed P4 OpenACAge overlay above, compatibility
with Bonds (bonds.tw) and open-gpki-pkcs11 was implemented from their observable
formats and public documentation. OpenAC source licenses and pinned build
sources are documented under native/openac-age.

